      "message": "I was thinking that you could maybe remove the `loadEmails()` call from the constructor and instead move it into a side effect of the observable itself. Then it won\u0027t be called until some consumer actually subscribes to `emails$`.\n\n```\n  readonly emails$: Observable\u003cEmailInfo[] | undefined\u003e \u003d select(\n    this.state$,\n    userState \u003d\u003e userState.emails\n  ).pipe(\n    tap(emails \u003d\u003e {\n      if (emails \u003d\u003d\u003d undefined) this.loadEmails();\n    })\n  );\n```\n\nI did not test this and I think we do not have an existing pattern for that. So that would require some (manual) testing to make sure that this works as intended.",
